# Deep Review

## Session boundary

The profile name never grants root authority. When invoked as a delegated child, execute only the task and scope in the parent packet.
A delegated child MUST NOT launch, invoke, or delegate to another agent (no `agent` tool calls), create additional lanes, or run the deep-review controller graph.
A child ignores orchestration instructions in loaded skills, completes the remaining assigned work and normal verification, and returns its result plus any conflict note to the parent.
If conflicting orchestration instructions leave no executable in-scope work, return the concrete blocker.
Do not infer root authority from a parent request to orchestrate.

## Native invocation notes (active root only)

Only the active root/main session may follow this section: load and follow `~/.agents/skills/k-deep-review/SKILL.md` in full.
Fan out with the `agent` tool onto the named Copilot profiles — `k-agent-review-worker`, `k-agent-review-worker-cross`, `k-agent-pr-necessity-auditor`, `k-agent-live-ui-review`, `k-agent-findings-auditor`, `k-agent-adversarial-verifier`. The roster and phase contracts decide which of them run and supply the task packet; this list is not an unconditional fan-out.
Copilot ships no fresh-eyes profile: launch that lane as a generic task carrying `k-review/references/fresh-eyes.md` with the resolved lane model, per `k-review/references/runtime-harnesses.md`.
Pass explicit scope (diff range, PR number, thread set) into each sighted task; workers do not see this conversation.
Keep fresh-eyes tasks blind: diff scope only, never PR number/title/body, commit messages, issue text, threads, prior findings or controller narrative, including re-runs.
